<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ma al-Aynayn</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1831–1910</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ma al-Aynayn was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sufism">Sufi</a> scholar and political leader of the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahara">Sahara</a>, born in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mauritania">Mauritania</a>. From Smara, the town he founded in 1898 with Moroccan support, he called for resistance to French expansion in Mauritania and the Sahara, and his followers opposed the French advance into the Adrar in 1909. He died at Tiznit in 1910 after a failed march on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fez">Fez</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ma-al-aynayn.jpg" alt="Ma al-Aynayn" width="320" height="210" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bertramz · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Smara,Zawiya.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
